  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nThis Weekend: Current satellite imagery depicts mid-level clouds\nentering the region. This may prevent temperatures from reaching \nthe forecast low temperature tonight. Cloud cover should persist \nuntil Saturday evening with clearing beginning Sunday. Expect\nnear-average temperatures with highs in the low 30s/upper 40s\nthrough the weekend. Gusty conditions are anticipated Saturday \nmorning through the evening. A Lake Wind Advisory has been issued\nfor Fort Peck Lake, in effect from 6 AM Saturday to 4 PM \nSaturday. Current NW flow aloft with weak troughing elevate PoPs \nthrough Saturday night as a cold front drapes across our region, \nexiting to our SSE on Saturday night. Expect gusty winds \nassociated with the front to subside by Saturday night. \nNortheastern portions of Montana have the best chance of seeing \nany rain/snow tonight through Saturday night, though any \naccumulations will remain negligible and/or trace. The synoptic \npattern will be transitioning to ridging by Sunday, associated \nwith high pressure. This will dry out the area with above-average \ntemperatures expected. A weather system moves into the area Monday\nto bring isolated chances of mixed precipitation. Thereafter, \nweak troughing conditions to bring cooler temperatures on Monday \nand possible rain/snow may be observed. If any precipitation \noccurs, accumulations likely to remain trace. \n\nTuesday onward: Weak troughing transitioning to ridging \nconditions are expected to persist dry, seasonably warmer \ntemperatures. The above-average temperatures are also tied to a \nblocking pattern in the flow by late next week. Current ensemble \nmodel guidance begins to disagree Wednesday with ensembles showing\na high spread in potential outcomes, in terms of timing. Above-\naverage temperatures should persist through next week with the \npassage of a warm front on Tuesday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\n\nThe only change this cycle was modifying NBM winds to NBM10/NBM90\nto accurately depict winds. \n\n- Confidence for above average temperatures is HIGH through \n  Sunday night.\n\n- Confidence is MODERATE (50%) from Tuesday onward.\n\n- Confidence in above-average temperatures is HIGH (75%) Tuesday\n  onward.\n\n- Confidence is LOW (20%-30%) for precipitation chances on Monday.\n\n- Confidence for gusty conditions on Saturday is HIGH (90%).\n\nFINDLEY",
